M6 ships the FIRST PLUGIN under loam's contribution-based
extension protocol, lifting the protocol from
"demonstrated-internally-only" (workspace-bootstrap is the only
package shipping `loam.bootstrap.contributions` entry-points
pre-M6) to "proven-end-to-end-from-outside-bootstrap-tree" (M6's
`plugins/dev-sdlc/` is the first external contributor). v0.2+
plugins inherit the pattern.

Plugin capability set at v0.1.0:

  1. ODD-shaped 5-stage workflow (research → spec → plan → build
     → review/verify) with per-stage artefact templates under
     `<project>/<stage>/<slug>.md` and structural gate enforcement
     (objective + AC presence required before stage advance).
  2. Stage-bound scope-of-work + objective-tracker integration —
     each stage advance creates a child scope under the project
     + a per-stage objective with ACs.
  3. Methodology opt-out via `--methodology=tdd|bdd|adhoc` flag
     preserving an internal ODD mirror at
     `<project>/.dev-sdlc-odd-mirror.yaml` (per Idea 3's "opt-out
     and imported projects keep an internal ODD representation").
  4. `loam project ...` CLI subcommand surface — five operator
     verbs (`new`, `status`, `advance`, `list`, `gate`) registered
     as subcommands of the unified `loam` CLI.
  5. Persona-invocable Python API at `loam.plugins.dev_sdlc.api`
     exposing `start_project`, `advance_stage`, `project_status`,
     `list_projects`, `gate_check`.
  6. Workspace-bootstrap contribution + manifest opt-in —
     `DevSdlcContribution` registered under
     `loam.bootstrap.contributions` entry-point group; workspace's
     `bootstrap.yaml` opts in via the `dev_sdlc` name string.
  7. `/start-project` Claude skill at
     `plugins/dev-sdlc/skills/start-project.md` (D-Q.M6.4 ship per
     owner ruling; conditional AC.OSS-M6.9).
  8. Per-project state in workspace-local SQLite at
     `<workspace>/.loam/dev-sdlc.sqlite` (single source of truth);
     `<project>/.dev-sdlc.yaml` is a derived human-readable mirror.

Critical structural finding (recorded at plan-authoring time):
M6 is the FIRST EXTERNAL contributor to workspace-bootstrap's
`loam.bootstrap.contributions` entry-point group. Pre-M6, the
only package shipping entries under that group was
`loam-workspace-bootstrap` itself (per
`framework/workspace-bootstrap/pyproject.toml` lines 37-53). M6
establishes the cross-package pattern; v0.2+ plugins inherit the
cheaper landing.

Subcommand-discovery mechanism (NEW at M6): the unified `loam`
CLI gains a `loam.cli.subcommands` entry-point group, symmetric
to bootstrap's pattern. Plugin's `pyproject.toml` ships
`[project.entry-points."loam.cli.subcommands"]` with `project =
"loam.plugins.dev_sdlc.cli:build_project_subcommand"`.
`loam_cli.cli.main` iterates the entry-points at startup +
invokes each `build_*` callable to register the subcommand
parser. Identical pattern to `framework/workspace-bootstrap/src/loam/workspace_bootstrap/discovery.py:_resolve_entrypoint`.

Plugin contribution metadata: `phase=after_orchestrator_ready`,
`after=('primary_persona','objective_tracker','scope_of_work')` —
plugin reads these host surfaces at construction time. Plugin is
non-load-bearing for orchestrator startup; it registers with
persona's command surface after orchestrator is ready.

Plugin tree placement at `plugins/dev-sdlc/` per master plan
§13 D-Q.OSS.5 + plan §10 D-Q.M6.1: establishes the plugin-tree
pattern at v0.1.0; v0.2+ plugins land at `plugins/<name>/` with
cheaper structural cost. Alternative `framework/dev-sdlc/`
rejected — conflates "core harness components" with "optional
plugin extensions" + forces plugin #2 to make the plugin-tree
decision under publishing pressure.

Partition manifest extension (M2 contract): M6 extends
`framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/publish-mode-manifest.yaml`
`audit_roots:` to add `plugins/` + `dev_and_public:` to add
`glob: "plugins/dev-sdlc/**"`. Synthesis includes the plugin in
the public artefact per AC.OSS-M6.8.

